## Why This Is Asked
Tests streaming algorithm intuition and amortized reasoning. Detecting heavy hitters with bounded memory on a growing stream is a common interview topic; Misra–Gries provides deterministic guarantees with simple updates.

## Key Concepts
- Misra–Gries heavy-hitters
- Choice of k = floor(1/phi) + 1 to bound missed items
- Amortized O(1) per element, O(k) memory
- Trade-offs: larger k reduces false positives but uses more memory

## Code Example
```javascript
class MGHeavyHitters {
  constructor(k) {
    this.k = k;
    this.counters = new Map();
  }
  update(x) {
    if (this.counters.has(x)) {
      this.counters.set(x, this.counters.get(x) + 1);
      return;
    }
    if (this.counters.size < this.k) {
      this.counters.set(x, 1);
      return;
    }
    for (const [key, val] of Array.from(this.counters)) {
      if (val === 1) this.counters.delete(key);
      else this.counters.set(key, val - 1);
    }
  }
  candidates() { return Array.from(this.counters.keys()); }
}
```

